---
source: crates/news/tests/cli.rs
expression: "stdout_of(&[\"--help\"])"
---
News agent toolbox. Every command prints one JSON envelope on stdout: {"ok":true,"data":…,"warnings":[],"truncated":false} or {"ok":false,"error":{…}}. Exit codes: 0 ok, 2 usage, 3 not found, 4 conflict or precondition, 5 retryable, 6 validation failed, 7 gated, 10 internal. Schemas: news schema <command>.

Usage: news [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  version      Print the CLI version as JSON
  db           Database: migrations and status
  discover     Run source connectors; store new candidates
  plan         Score, cluster and select stories for a run (the Budget)
  fetch        Download a story's source files and API data
  parse        Parse a story's snapshots into data points and text blocks
  brief        Build the brief for a story
  components   List the component index, one line per component
  component    One component's props, data shape and example
  related      Related pages and entities for a story
  save         Store a Copy (page draft) for a story
  render       Render a story's page bundle
  check        Run the code checks on a story's page
  publish      Publish a story's page (G tier)
  update       Load a published page for revision
  prune        Delete working files for published items
  stats        Run and coverage summary
  home         Home page curation (Frontpage)
  run          Chief: preset runs and their status (read-only; Board starts and controls runs)
  standing     Standing: Karthik's versioned settings (read-only; Board changes them)
  service      The Bureau service
  jobs         Dispatch: the job queue
  ai           Ghost: contracts for every AI step
  sources      Contacts: the source registry
  calendar     Diary: the release calendar
  stories      Taster: stories
  scores       Nose: scores and weights
  entities     Roster: entities
  eval         Critic: evaluations
  review       Huddle: the weekly review
  corrections  Errata: reader error reports
  schema       Input and output JSON Schemas of a command
  help         Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --limit <N>
          Return at most N list items (default 20; `jobs claim`: how many to claim, default 1)

      --fields <A,B>
          Keep only these keys of each item, comma-separated

      --cursor <CURSOR>
          Continue a truncated list from its next_cursor

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version
